INFO:
	- double indexes in casadi does not work (e.g. ### SX a(l:1); a(Slice(l1,l2))(1) = b ### does not assign correctly at a(l1+1))
	- thunder needs to be reinstalled if thunder_robot_template is modified
	- load_conf read and parse the configuration file, load_par read the file that has the same structure as the internal args map, same for save
	- thunder take the file <robot>.yaml that contains the configuration of the robot
	- thunder take thunder_robot and rename it to thunder_<robot>, changing inside the necessary. Then copy it to generatedFiles
	- thunder generates the <robot>_inertial_REG.yaml from the config file 
	- elastic and friction regressors implemented with jacobian
	kinematic convention:
		- T_w_0: Transformation from world to base
		- T_w_i: Transformation from world to link i
		- Links are numbered from 0 to n where n is the number of joints
		- Joints are numbered from 1 to n
		- Joint i connects link i-1 to link i
		- Link i is solidal to joint i
		- Link n is the end-effector
		- Link 0 is considered only in case of moving base robot (not ready)
	version update in:
		- README.md
		- CHANGELOG.md
		- pyproject.toml
		- CMakeLists.txt
		- thunder_main.cpp
